&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49461066</guid><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 07:17:51 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Ask HN: What do you do when your AI coding agent is doing its job?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49461055</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I am into my early 50s and recently diagnosed with adult ADHD and maladaptive daydreaming.&lt;p&gt;I realized that I have struggled with it since I was 16.&lt;p&gt;I always wanted to work in programming, but it never worked out for me. I am now in a coding-adjacent job, as a sysadmin (Windows).&lt;p&gt;I have recently started doing coding - some side/hobby projects - with the help of AI. But I realize that when the Codex is doing its work, I kind of zone out or get busy with something else, and it is difficult to return to the task. So, I try to keep the coding sessions more interactive. I always ask Codex to go one step at a time. It is not very efficient, and it doesn't always work - also impractical sometimes.&lt;p&gt;I would like to know what other HN users generally do when their coding agents are doing their job.&lt;/p&gt;
